1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,960
Try turning on the lights and stepping back.

2
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:28,460
like someone calling out to you,
after the rain has stopped.

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:35,340
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand by Gājan.

4
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,380
The strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,740
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,140
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow above their eyes too.

10
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,700
Try turning at that corner.

11
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,920
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,840
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:34,620
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,060
A hellish life of misfortune.

16
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,900
Even if it's sickening,
I bought a huge amount today, in GI form.

17
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:48,580
I'm going to make the
inside of the room spotless!

18
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:50,600
Just one more step to our dorm!

19
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:51,960
What?

20
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:03,120
Wh-wh-what's this?! The dorm's gone!

21
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,360
Ryo-san, you're here?

22
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:08,180
Of course I'm here! What's going on, auntie?

23
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:09,660
They're rebuilding it.

24
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:11,020
Rebuilding it?

25
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:15,780
The other men's dorm at Katsushika Station
got caught in a land readjustment project.

26
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:19,520
So it's been decided to
merge it with our dorm.

27
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,400
So that's why they're rebuilding.

28
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,500
Yes, because the number
of residents is going up.

29
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,460
Yeah, yeah, but you can't just
do it all of a sudden, can you?

30
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:28,663
Ryo-san,

31
00:02:28,713 --> 00:02:32,060
it's been posted on the bulletin
board for three months already!

32
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,520
Did our Ryo even have a bulletin board?

33
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,680
It was there.

34
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,340
Well, this is a problem.
Where are we supposed to live?

35
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,920
Everyone seems to be renting apartments
or staying at friends' houses.

36
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,060
I'm about to go to my daughter's place now.

37
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:48,480
Well then, see you in two months, Ryo-san.

38
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,720
Yeah, take care.

39
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:53,660
Dear me,
I'd better find a place to sleep too.

40
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,600
Stay at my place?

41
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:58,620
Please, I'm counting on you.

42
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,640
Sorry.

43
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,280
Starting tomorrow,
an Arab ambassador is touring Japan,

44
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,580
and he's going to be staying at my place for a while,
so it's a bit...

45
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,360
What?

46
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,860
Are you saying that if I stay,
I'd bring shame on Japan?

47
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,900
It's not that, exactly.

48
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,060
Then what is it?

49
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:13,820
Didn't Ryo-san already go home?

50
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,600
Terai-kun!

51
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,880
Perfect timing, you're back.

52
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:17,640
Actually,

53
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,360
Wait a second.

54
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:22,360
Your commute takes about
three and a half hours, right?

55
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,640
Yeah, it does.

56
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,620
So what?

57
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:25,860
Nahaha.

58
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:26,840
Nothing.

59
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,020
Reiko-chan...

60
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:31,780
You haven't even said anything yet!

61
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,240
No way, no way, no way!

62
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:37,380
What are you thinking,
wanting to crash at a single woman's place?

63
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,980
If I had to live with Ryo-chan
for two whole months...

64
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,360
I'd rather live with cockroaches.

65
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:43,800
That's going a bit far, isn't it?

66
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,000
Who would ever live with you?

67
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,100
What's wrong, Ryo-san?

68
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,980
The dorm's being rebuilt,
so I've lost my place to live.

69
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,820
Well, that's rough.

70
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:58,700
But don't worry,
I won't be a bother at your place.

71
00:03:59,540 --> 00:03:59,980
Thanks.

72
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,440
Chief.

73
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,860
I'm busy, I'm busy.

74
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,940
Reiko-kun, this one's fine,
so hand me those papers over there.

75
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:10,460
Yes.

76
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,220
Chief.

77
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:12,920
Chief.

78
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,220
Chief.

79
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,320
Chief.

80
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,300
Here you go.

81
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:16,760
Thanks.

82
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,480
That's the one, that's the one!

83
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,500
Chief.

84
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,880
Chief, please listen to me.

85
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,980
You fool!

86
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,400
Well, at least hear me out.

87
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,600
No, no, no.

88
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:35,100
Two months at the Chief's house would be simply wonderful,
wouldn't it?

89
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:38,180
Then the storage room is empty.

90
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:41,760
Bring a blanket in there
and it'll make a fine home.

91
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:46,020
My subordinate is suffering, and you
can still come out with jokes like that?

92
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,700
I'm not joking.

93
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:51,780
With more life force than a cockroach,
you'd be fine sleeping rough, right?

94
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,060
No, I'm not fine with that!

95
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,900
It's close by,
and there's no worry about being late.

96
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:02,060
Lately, bōsōzoku gather at
the park behind us every night.

97
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,920
Maybe I'll join a biker
gang and go on a rampage.

98
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,220
You haven't got a penny to your name.
How are you going to buy a motorbike?

99
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,060
A bōsōzoku on a Sarinko

100
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,360
Anyway, I don't want to hear about it.

101
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:15,180
I see. Fine, I understand.

102
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:17,040
If it comes to this, I'll really go bad.

103
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,160
And when I get arrested, I'll say this:

104
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,760
"Look how far I was driven into crime."

105
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,540
It's all the fault of Ohara from the Kōen-mae police box,
you know.

106
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:28,260
If you'd let me stay at your place back then,
I wouldn't have gone astray.

107
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,880
I'll rant and rave that
it's all Chief Ohara's fault!

108
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,880
Ryo-chan, you're totally capable of that.

109
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:36,860
Yeah, that's true.

110
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:40,680
If that happens,
the Chief could lose his job too.

111
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:44,240
Fine, Ryotsu. Come stay at my place.

112
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,420
Thank you! I knew you'd understand if I asked, Chief.
You're a man of justice.

113
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:53,960
Where's the justice? But you'll be treated like family,
not like a boarder.

114
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:56,480
Thank you in advance.

115
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:01,280
From JR, then the facility,
then the bus, then on foot.

116
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,200
How can you even bring
yourself to commute every day?

117
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,300
Stop your complaining and just follow me.

118
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:09,380
You'll be commuting to the station on this same route for the next two months,
you know.

119
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,300
Yeah, yeah.

120
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,740
I'm home!

121
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:16,340
Welcome, Mr. Maruotsu.

122
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,960
Madam, it's been a while.

123
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,580
Well, come in, come in.

124
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,940
I'm not here as a guest.

125
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:24,440
Starting today,
I'll be staying with you for two months.

126
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,860
Thank you for having me.

127
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:30,420
Not at all. Please make yourself at home.

128
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,320
What are you talking about?

129
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:34,700
Free lodging, and on top of that you make yourself at home?
That's a real nuisance.

130
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,500
Dear

131
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:39,020
Put up with it, Kankichi Ryotsu.
It's only two months of patience.

132
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:41,460
We'll have dinner before the bath today.

133
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:42,860
Yes, understood.

134
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:45,180
What's your favorite food, Ryotsu-san?

135
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,240
Yes, anything.

136
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:46,640
Hey.

137
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,180
Yes.

138
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,260
Don't ask Ryotsu about every little thing.

139
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:51,060
Just think of him as air.

140
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,500
Don't be picky about what you like or dislike, okay?
Just remember it.

141
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,180
It's time for the news.

142
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:01,380
That bath after a delicious
dinner was so relaxing.

143
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:03,740
Ryo-san, you want some tea or not?

144
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:05,460
Sorry, I'll have some.

145
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,100
Don't bother making him any.

146
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,380
Ryotsu, make your own tea,
for crying out loud.

147
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,200
Yes, yes.

148
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,600
Sorry about that.

149
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,300
It's fine, it's fine.

150
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,100
I have no idea what you're talking about.

151
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,460
Chief, do you think this show is any good?

152
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,180
That's not the point.

153
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:24,880
As a police officer,
you should know this much.

154
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:31,540
Do you always watch that kind of programme?

155
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:32,980
No, not at all.

156
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:37,300
I'd like to watch NHK too,
but for some reason the reception is poor.

157
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:40,400
This is a good chance. Watch NHK here.

158
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,900
I suddenly feel dizzy...

159
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,240
Yoko-san, are you all right?

160
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,300
I'm fine.

161
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:47,600
You must be tired after such a long day.

162
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,660
Shouldn't you rest now?

163
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,740
I see.

164
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,840
What a shame. I really wanted to watch NHK.

165
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,000
Go to bed already.

166
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,840
Right, then I'll excuse myself.

167
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,130
Honestly,

168
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:05,140
our TV tastes are the complete opposite of the Chief's,
you know.

169
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:08,840
If it's this early, I need a drink or two.

170
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:10,300
I can't sleep.

171
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:13,540
Pocket Bin, you're my only friend.

172
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:17,380
Honestly, having a stubborn boss
means the people under him suffer.

173
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:18,900
Hey, Ryotsu.

174
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:23,060
I'll wake you early tomorrow
so you don't be late.

175
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,180
Just go to sleep already.

176
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:31,520
It's like being watched
every moment I'm at home.

177
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:34,160
I'm at a disadvantage here, aren't I?

178
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,820
Hey, Yoshi, get up!

179
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,800
Is it morning already?

180
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,880
How long are you going to sleep, honestly?

181
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:48,780
When you're up,
fold your futon and come to the courtyard.

182
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:54,060
It's still dark. What time is it?

183
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:56,480
It's not even 4 o'clock yet!

184
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:59,020
Honestly, old people wake up so early.

185
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:00,420
How many times have I told you?

186
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:01,460
Coming right now!

187
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,760
61 62 63 64 65

188
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,580
Swing it back further, all the way!

189
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:09,580
68, 69, 70

190
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:12,340
Why? What are you doing?

191
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,240
Your hips aren't in it, your hips!

192
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,660
Alright, let's take a short break.

193
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,760
What a useless sloth you are.

194
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:21,520
Practice swings right after waking up?
That's absurd, honestly.

195
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,600
The sun hasn't even come out yet.

196
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:28,420
I have to catch the 6 o'clock bus, so I
have to get up this early or I won't make it.

197
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,500
If it's the 6 o'clock bus,
getting up at 5 should be plenty!

198
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:35,940
Even an idiot who's a police officer
must always keep his body trained.

199
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:38,120
I do a hundred of these every day.

200
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:41,520
A young man like you should
easily manage two hundred.

201
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:45,140
Fine, I'll show you I can do three hundred,
not just two hundred!

202
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:46,940
Well said! Then do it!

203
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:51,693
75, 76, 127, 128,

204
00:09:51,743 --> 00:09:54,301
129, 130, 172,

205
00:09:54,351 --> 00:09:56,881
173, 174, 203,

206
00:09:56,931 --> 00:09:59,511
204, 205, 206,

207
00:09:59,561 --> 00:10:02,079
207, 209, 210,

208
00:10:02,129 --> 00:10:04,696
211, 250, 251,

209
00:10:04,746 --> 00:10:07,289
252, 295, 296,

210
00:10:07,339 --> 00:10:10,580
297, 298, 299, 300

211
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,680
Chief, I'm done.

212
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,460
Good, that'll do.

213
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:20,960
Alright, time to eat!
Food tastes best after exercise.

214
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:23,680
Ugh... is there still more?

215
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:29,140
Look at that. The weeds have grown quite a bit.
I was thinking of pulling them out.

216
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:33,800
Is that so? Well, good luck.
I'll go wash off the sweat first.

217
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,340
In a case like this,
someone should volunteer, though.

218
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:40,360
Like a man who's just eating free meals,
for example.

219
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:42,840
Fine, fine. I'll do it, okay? I'll do it.

220
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:46,300
Thanks.
I didn't expect you to do it on your own.

221
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:50,460
No, no, no...
Did I force you into something?

222
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:51,720
Damn it!

223
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,340
Ryo-chan, are you all right?

224
00:10:56,880 --> 00:11:00,220
You've only been boarding at
the Chief's home for a week,

225
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,900
and you already look terribly worn out.

226
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:05,400
Now you know how hard the long commute is,
Ryo-san.

227
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:08,180
It's not just the grueling commute.

228
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:10,400
Every morning I'm dragged
out of bed at 4 a.m.

229
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,760
and worked to the bone.

230
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,440
Dad, let's just call a taxi.

231
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:18,160
Come on.
Ryotsu can handle this much, no problem.

232
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,240
Hey, Ryotsu.

233
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,560
Heh heh, y-you're absolutely right.

234
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:25,860
On top of that, I'm forced to go
along with the Chief's hobbies too.

235
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:28,380
Chief, let's go to bed already.

236
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:32,300
No, I told you we're staying up until
the ten-match contest is over tonight.

237
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:35,240
Ote, it's Ryotsu's ote!

238
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,500
But take whatever you like,

239
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,260
please take it with you.

240
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:47,100
On top of that, try being in my shoes,
unable to go to the horse races or pachinko.

241
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,500
Sounds like it's going to
build up a lot of stress.

242
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:50,640
I wonder if he'll last two months.

243
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:52,000
Probably not.

244
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,800
Just you watch,
I'll definitely get out of this life.

245
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:01,620
And now, tomorrow's weather.

246
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,540
Has Ryotsu gone to bed already?

247
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:06,580
Looks like it.
He said he's getting up early.

248
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:08,880
I see. Then I'll turn in too.

249
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:11,660
I've got to whip him into shape again tomorrow,
after all.

250
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,880
Since he showed up,
things have gotten even busier.

251
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:23,400
Honestly, Dad, you seem to be having a
great time every day since Ryo-san arrived.

252
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,120
Ma'am.

253
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:28,000
Is it all right if I
watch a show I want to see?

254
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,680
Please, go ahead.

255
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:35,080
At last, I can watch my favourite programme.

256
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:38,660
Ryo-san, would you like a cup?
Do you want some?

257
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:39,860
Are you sure?

258
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:43,600
Here you go.

259
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,000
Thank you.

260
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,760
Ah, that's good.

261
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:51,300
Don't worry, Dad's fine.

262
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:54,780
He's been falling asleep really easily lately.
He's out cold.

263
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:55,835
I see.

264
00:12:55,885 --> 00:12:59,460
But won't he suddenly slide
that door open and come out?

265
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:03,000
Ryo-san,
you must really be scared of your dad.

266
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,000
"Scared" doesn't even begin to cover it.

267
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,540
I'm like a frog under a snake's glare.

268
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,320
Well, hahaha. Here, have another cup.

269
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:15,080
I didn't think I'd get
to drink openly like this.

270
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:18,580
It's not fair that only
Dad gets a nightcap, is it?

271
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:19,483
You know,

272
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:23,260
Dad's really happy that
Ryo-san came to visit.

273
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,340
The Chief?

274
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:26,000
I'm their only daughter, you know?

275
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:28,720
Apparently he really wanted a son.

276
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:33,260
Now that Ryo-san's here,
I bet he sees you like a son.

277
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:35,860
Hey, don't tell me that scary Chief...

278
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:38,200
S-sorry.

279
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:42,840
It's just sleep talk.
He often gets angry like that about Ryo-san.

280
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:45,060
Even asleep, all he thinks about is work.

281
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:48,160
Wow, that scared me.
Even asleep, he's shoving people aside.

282
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:51,920
Honestly, if he were my father,
I'd never have a moment's peace.

283
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:52,560
Honestly.

284
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,200
How about a drink?

285
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,060
Once in a while won't hurt, right?

286
00:13:58,060 --> 00:14:00,920
Well, I suppose I'll have just one.

287
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,300
That's the spirit!

288
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:05,900
Here you go.

289
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:06,400
Thanks.

290
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:10,887
Well, you're really putting it away.

291
00:14:10,937 --> 00:14:12,640
Let's have another one.

292
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:16,360
Tonight, let's drink till dawn and pour
out all our complaints about the Chief.

293
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:16,740
Well.

294
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:23,620
What? You didn't even
kiss until the wedding?

295
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:27,720
Not only that,
he wouldn't even hold my hand, your father.

296
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,840
So the Chief was
stiff-headed even back then.

297
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:32,980
That's his only redeeming quality,
after all.

298
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:37,140
But how have you managed to stay with
a hardhead like that for nearly 30 years?

299
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:38,380
Doesn't it suffocate you?

300
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:40,580
We're used to it by now.

301
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:43,960
But it would be a relief
if he softened up a little.

302
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:47,140
That hardhead will never change, you know.

303
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:50,320
Well, yes, maybe he really never will.

304
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,480
It's morning!

305
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,020
How long are you going to sleep? Get up!

306
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:02,080
You reek of booze.

307
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:03,860
Get up!

308
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,540
I can't drink anymore...

309
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:08,460
Get up! Get up!

310
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,220
That's cold!

311
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:15,600
Are you awake now?

312
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:18,140
What are you doing, Chief!

313
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:19,440
You're really trying to kill me!

314
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:19,900
Shut up!

315
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:24,080
How dare you sneak drinks as a freeloader!

316
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:29,060
But yesterday your wife insisted on drinking,
so I kept her company.

317
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,500
What? My wife?

318
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,840
Yes, she was crying while she drank.

319
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:36,140
Why didn't my wife join in?

320
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:38,820
You're just too rigid, Chief.

321
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:42,120
I heard you didn't even hold her
hand during your engagement, right?

322
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:47,960
Of course I didn't! Unlike young people today,
back then that was common sense.

323
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,660
That's not all, you know.

324
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:56,660
He's always giving orders in that commanding tone,
and she wishes he'd loosen up a bit.

325
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,520
Your wife was pleading
with tears in her eyes.

326
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:01,320
Dad.

327
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:07,180
Dad, I'm heading out first, since I'm going
shopping and then stopping by city hall.

328
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:10,920
I've already got your meal ready,
so please take care of yourself.

329
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:13,340
City hall.

330
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:15,780
I wonder if they're going
to pick up divorce forms.

331
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:16,360
What?

332
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:22,260
I hear there are a lot of wives lately who bring
up divorce right after their husbands retire.

333
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:25,080
Not my husband, of all people.

334
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:28,960
The wife who divorces takes the retirement money
as alimony instead,

335
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,240
and throws her husband out like garbage,
they say.

336
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,360
Apparently,
that's called retirement divorce.

337
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,840
Retirement divorce.

338
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,400
Retirement divorce.

339
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:41,440
What do I need to do
so I don't get divorced?

340
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:45,240
First and foremost, you need to
soften that stubborn head of yours.

341
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:49,720
How do I soften it? Tell me.

342
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,500
First, this. This one.

343
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,200
So what if I don't?

344
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,800
You should stop fiddling with bonsai.

345
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,720
What, no way!

346
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,000
Chief.

347
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,140
You're the one who asked me to
teach you how to soften your head,

348
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:03,940
Chief.

349
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:07,280
Honestly,
I don't care whether you get divorced

350
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,780
or whatever you do, Chief.

351
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:10,740
Ryotsu!

352
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:13,340
Fine, I'll do anything, so please help me!

353
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:14,620
Alright, I understand.

354
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:16,760
So no more of this every morning,
either, right?

355
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:18,680
Of course, who needs this anyway!

356
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,900
Now the tables have completely turned!

357
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,960
Alright, let's go with this jacket.

358
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,200
The pants are fine like this.

359
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,540
Okay, now just bring the sneakers and a hat.

360
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,160
Yes.

361
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:36,540
Why do I have to dress like this?

362
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:40,900
To become a flexible-minded person,
we start by remodeling your appearance.

363
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:41,860
But...

364
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:45,280
Your wife said she wants
you to dress younger.

365
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,020
Still, this is...

366
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,840
Retirement divorce.

367
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:51,260
Maybe I'll come along too.

368
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:02,040
Ryotsu, everyone's staring at you.

369
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:05,460
That's because Chief,
you're dressed fashionably for your age.

370
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,540
They're looking at you with approval.

371
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,420
That's not how it looks to me.

372
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:11,620
Ryotsu, you really are...

373
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:14,400
Retirement divorce.

374
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,920
Retirement divorce.

375
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,240
Retirement divorce.

376
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:23,500
I win.

377
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:27,240
Then, Chief, how about we make a little bet?

378
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:28,700
Ready?

379
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:31,740
Whether the next person to come around that corner
Translation>
is a man or a woman,

380
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:33,160
let's bet our evening sake.

381
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,960
Then I'll go first.

382
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,460
Let's start with a woman.

383
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,840
I'll take a man.

384
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,600
Alright, first round,
one bottle of sake for the winner.

385
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:43,540
Alright, then next I'll pick a woman.

386
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,580
Then I'll go with a man.

387
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,780
Yes, it's a man!

388
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,420
Second bottle of sake, I win!

389
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:51,700
Alright, a woman again next.

390
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:56,140
You're really getting into this, Chief.
Aren't you quite the gambler?

391
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:58,360
Shut up. Anyway, I'm going with a woman.

392
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,120
Yeah, yeah.

393
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:04,560
Yes! A woman, a woman! Ryotsu, I win!

394
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:09,300
Looks like I won this time too, it seems.

395
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,840
What happened, Dad? What's with that outfit?

396
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:16,500
Well, I said I didn't want to, but...

397
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:19,980
But somehow you look
younger and it suits you!

398
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:21,640
See? Told you.

399
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,420
Well, I'm not so past it yet, am I?

400
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:28,220
Dad, you really are something.

401
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,620
Flatter a pig and it'll climb a tree

402
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,380
Mom, tea.

403
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:34,040
Yes.

404
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,120
Here you go.

405
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:39,780
Dad, aren't you having
your evening drink tonight?

406
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:41,540
There's a reason.

407
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:45,260
Ryotsu, the news. Switch it to NHK.

408
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,460
Hey, on Sundays it's Fuji TV, right?

409
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,400
Chibi Maruko-chan, then Sazae-san,

410
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,180
then the Kochikame anime,

411
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:59,900
then Super Night Music Fair, then the Central Racing Digest.
That's how a proper Sunday night is spent, right?

412
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:00,940
Honestly, you...

413
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:04,900
First you have to watch anime
to loosen up your head, dear.

414
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:06,680
Yes.

415
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:14,180
Don't you start too! Anyway, I can't settle
down unless I watch the 7 o'clock NHK news.

416
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:16,240
Chief, with your retirement...

417
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:20,200
Yeah, maybe anime isn't
so bad once in a while.

418
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,000
Right?

419
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:25,640
Ugh, this is unbearable.

420
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,780
I'm going to bed tonight.

421
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:30,260
What on earth has gotten into you, dear?

422
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:35,580
Well, sometimes you just want to skip
your nightcap and bath and go to bed early.

423
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:38,060
Speaking of which, what about you, ma'am?

424
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:43,740
Chief, these days you can't even sing Dragon
Ash at karaoke without your wife disliking you.

425
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:46,940
You should also skateboard and
show a younger side of yourself.

426
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:50,640
And if you could use the internet,
she might look at you in a new light.

427
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:53,960
That's right, ma'am, why not go to
an amusement park once in a while?

428
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:57,280
She said she'd like to do something
like bungee jumping with you.

429
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,120
I wonder what's gotten into the Chief.

430
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:04,560
He's just gone limp.

431
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:06,460
Yeah, compared to that...

432
00:21:07,780 --> 00:21:10,940
Ryo-san over there looks so cheerful.

433
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:11,460
Yes.

434
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,580
It must be some kind of mistake.

435
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:26,160
Well, we did receive a call from Mr. Daijirō Ohara saying he wanted a car,
so I've brought the brochures and the estimate.

436
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,300
Hey, Daijirō-san.

437
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:28,720
Let's see, let's see.

438
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,460
Ryotsu, what's the meaning of this?

439
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:33,700
I thought it'd be convenient for your commute,
so I called.

440
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,340
Don't do things without permission.

441
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:39,200
Your wife said too,
"If you don't buy me a car, it's divorce!"

442
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:43,820
Don't lie! My wife is arranging the car,
so I'm not riding in one.

443
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:45,140
Is that so?

444
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:46,880
What kind of man are you?

445
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:51,120
That's enough! I won't have someone like you in my house!
Get out, effective today!

446
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:51,605
Fine,

447
00:21:51,655 --> 00:21:55,660
Fine! I don't want to stay in the
Chief's house a moment longer either!

448
00:21:55,780 --> 00:21:56,560
What?

449
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,440
What about the car...

450
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:01,280
Why are you following me?
Get out of here already!

451
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,040
I'll leave once I've gotten my things!

452
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:05,680
So that junk is your stuff!

453
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,806
Sorry for being junk, then.

454
00:22:07,856 --> 00:22:11,420
Not like I've got a fancy mansion
or belongings like this anyway!

455
00:22:12,020 --> 00:22:14,720
What's going on? You haven't
even turned on the entrance light?

456
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:19,840
Where have you been until this hour?

457
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:22,660
Isn't it just that the
divorce has come sooner?

458
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:23,660
W-what?

459
00:22:23,660 --> 00:22:26,800
Not my wife, no way.

460
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,620
When I'm late, she always makes sure

461
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:32,380
to have dinner ready.

462
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,720
If you really walk out,

463
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:37,260
N-no way.

464
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:39,460
Chief, I understand how you feel.

465
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:41,540
Let's drink the whole night tonight.

466
00:22:41,540 --> 00:22:42,760
Ryo-tsu!

467
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:45,300
What are you doing?

468
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:48,360
Ryo-tsu, you're a good guy.

469
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:49,780
Chief.

470
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:52,260
Come on, cheer up.

471
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:54,620
I'm home.

472
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,000
Mom.

473
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,940
Sorry I'm late.

474
00:22:57,940 --> 00:23:01,160
I went shopping on my bike today,
a bit of a trip out.

475
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:03,220
and I got a flat tire on the way.

476
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,320
Mom.

477
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:06,100
Mom.

478
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:08,080
I'm so glad you came back.

479
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:10,840
What happened to Dad?

480
00:23:10,840 --> 00:23:14,040
I thought for sure you'd been divorced and kicked out,
you know.

481
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:20,140
Of course, Dad. No matter what happens,
I'll stay by your side until we die.

482
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:26,060
Mom, but you went to Ryotsu crying,
saying you hate stubborn people, didn't you?

483
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:31,400
I did say that if only you were a little more flexible-minded,
but I didn't cry.

484
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:36,140
I'm just happy to be with
you as you are now, Dad.

485
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:37,940
Thanks, Mom.

486
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,800
No way, not in front of Ryo-san!

487
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:42,540
There.

488
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:44,580
Ryotsu!

489
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,640
You big liar, I won't forgive you!

490
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:51,080
But you said just now that he's a good guy!

491
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:53,760
I'll whip a loser like you
back into shape from scratch!

492
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:55,500
Just stay in this house forever!

493
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:59,520
No way, please have mercy on me!

494
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:05,540
I kicked the alarm clock and stubbed my pinky toe,
ouch ouch ouch!

495
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:13,760
Once I've drawn on my eyebrows, it's dance,
dance, dance all the way to the station!

496
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:19,580
On the train, my back to the road home,
I'm sure to doze off.

497
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:25,840
Another hard week, thanks for your work,
the strain is only natural.

498
00:24:27,140 --> 00:24:30,540
Bread basket in one hand, playing it cool.

499
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:33,280
Beef bowl, with extra sauce,
on a cloudy day.

500
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:36,620
The irritation from endless overtime,

501
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:40,240
gets cleared away by more irritation.

502
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:50,020
Every day's no problem,
once I've passed through a hot shower,

503
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:56,560
every day's no problem,
a mesh pillow restores my energy.

504
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:06,220
Every day's no problem,
I love this me just the way I am.

505
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:13,020
Every day's no brain,
Monday with hearts floating away.

506
00:25:13,460 --> 00:25:17,320
Mandeck, Mandeck, no brain.

507
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:22,660
The Chief, hopeless with machines,
bought a cell phone.

508
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:25,820
And sure enough, as I thought,
he can't use it at all.

509
00:25:25,820 --> 00:25:29,420
Chief, tools are meant to be used, not to be pushed around by them.
What are you doing?

510
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:31,500
The cell phone's gone?

511
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:33,460
It's not my fault.

512
00:25:33,460 --> 00:25:35,780
Next time: Cell Phone Panic!

513
00:25:36,220 --> 00:25:37,000
See you next time.

